# FMT-A regression fixture (Round XXXVI): the `Expr::UnaryOp` arm MUST
# wrap a binary operand whose precedence is lower than the unary op's
# operand bp (33). Without the wrap, `-(a + b)` re-emits as `-a + b`
# = `Add(Neg(a), b)` instead of the intended `Neg(Add(a, b))`.
#
# Pre-fix RED signature: `gg fmt` re-emitted `int r = -a + b` and
# running the reformatted file printed `1` instead of `-7`.
void main():
    int a = 3
    int b = 4
    int r = -(a + b)
    print(r)
